> These are some of the more compelling artifact YANIs that have been
> posted in a long time.  They only "suck" if you're a powergamer who
> won't ascend without Frost Brand or Grayswandir.

Here, you meant to say "effective" gamer.

The problem with adding any new artifact to the game is that there are
so many artifacts right now that are good, and can be wished for.  Plus,
wishes are relatively plentiful (blessed smoky potions, magic lamps,
guaranteed wand in the castle, fountain quaffing, thrones ... and that
doesn't even add in random wand/lamp/potion deathdrops or *gasp* farming.)

Thus, it makes no sense to add artifacts to the game that aren't at
least close to being on par with the current 'best' artifacts.  Right
now I tend to avoid sacrificing for artifacts until I've got the Castle
wand and know what I'll need to wish for; reflection, MR, and solid
armor is the first priority if any of those are missing, and _then_ i'll
consider an artifact.  If I have a wish to spare (and I probably will),
then I'm going top tier, and because I haven't generated any artifacts
myself, there's a strong possibility I'll succeed.

I've ascended with a +7 halberd before, and many Priests routinely
ascend with a +7 original mace.  Weaponry actually ISN'T as big a deal
as everyone makes it out to be as long as you have the appropriate other
tools.

That said, I agree that new artifact weaponry should probably be closer
to on par with Frost Brand than it should be to the Quest artifacts, and
I tend to not make a significant separation of the two in my mind since
the Quest artifacts can still be wished for.  But the point remains; I'm
not going to be happy finding any of those four on the ground before I
get to the Castle, and I'm certainly not going to start saccing in hopes
of getting one of those four as opposed to Orcrist or Giantslayer.  I
don't want to spend tons of time at the god-B-Q hoping for a good
weapon, so the most reliable means of obtaining an above-average weapon
remains the plain old wish.  And if I've gotta wish, I'm going top-tier.

Artifacts need to be good enough that I'm willing to throw away my +7
mace to pick them up and use them instead, if I find them on the ground
in Gehennom.

